  "Groups": [
    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "NOTL",
        "Description": "NOT reading (input A, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.375) of the shipped 'Logic Gate NOT-NAND' gate. Role in the 2-bit program counter: select inversion, NL = NOT(LOAD), feeding the count arms H0/H1 of the two bit multiplexers. LOAD also drives the load arms LD0/LD1 directly: the three unconnected pins share the persisted signal name LOAD, so one network toggle drives them without a waveguide. The whole PC composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate's truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction \u2014 there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here.",
        "Identifier": "group_0c2cda134f4e5a4fbe59de42ab15",
        "IdGuid": "0c2cda13-4f4e-5a4f-be59-de42ab152e97",
