    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "X",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A, B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped 'Logic Gate NOT-NAND' gate. Role in the 2-bit program counter: the XOR pivot X = NAND(C0, C1) of the high bit's increment \u2014 the same 4-NAND XOR the shipped 2-bit counter uses, here feeding the bit-1 multiplexer instead of the register directly. The whole PC composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate's truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction \u2014 there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here.",
        "Identifier": "group_918ad34dc500594ea30ce39b6c9b",
        "IdGuid": "918ad34d-c500-594e-a30c-e39b6c9b71f5",
