    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "REG0",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A, B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped 'Logic Gate NOT-NAND' gate, designated a register (issue #1098): the low count bit. Role in the 2-bit program counter: closes the bit-0 multiplexer, D0 = NAND(H0, LD0) = (INC0 AND NOT(LOAD)) OR (L0 AND LOAD). While the network settles, Y keeps reading the committed C0; only the clock Step samples D0 and commits it as the new C0 (D-semantics). The named output tap C0 (issue #1025) makes the bus view show the count. The whole PC composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate's truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction \u2014 there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here.",
        "Identifier": "group_bd561f80cbe45b8693bec0e7fe96",
